<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarayu River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sarayu is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the name given in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> tradition to the stretch of the Ghaghara that flows past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayodhya">Ayodhya</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>. It is mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a>, which places <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>'s city on its banks, and pilgrims bathe in it at Ayodhya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarayu-river.jpg" alt="Sarayu River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Digvijaysjanoti · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarju_Aarti_at_Bageshwar_(Cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
